<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    A value living only in a register piece no register name covers.
        sh_openpipe (gcc -O2):  mov rcx,rdi; call xpipe; test eax,eax
                                js done; ... done: ret
    The supplied xpipe body writes eax, so callee-body evidence proves the
    upper half of rax zero. This original case remains, but no longer needs
    an unknown upper-register piece.

    piece_return instead consumes a whole rax after wide_return, whose
    declared int4 result covers only eax while its body loads all of rax.
    The upper half remains outside that declaration: storage register 0x4,
    which no register name covers. Naming routed it to the global
    `dat_<addr>` arm because register is a processor space like ram, printing
    `return CONCAT44(dat_4,wide_return(p));` without declaring dat_4.
    The piece must instead be a local declared with its storage.

    Stage: P6 variable naming (ActionNameVars).  A strict fix with no
    option: #1 is the declared local, #2 the old global-looking name.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000" readonly="true">
